  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Initial release: container-backed SQL Server, application and stubbed dependencies for web timelines.\nWorth knowing up front:\n- A container reused across runs keeps whatever the previous run wrote, so SqlResetMode decides what happens to the database between runs - recreate it, run a reset script, or leave it alone.\n- Published ports bind to 127.0.0.1 rather than every interface, and the SQL Server password is generated per environment instead of being a constant shipped in the package. Use UseSqlPassword(...) to pin it, which a reused container needs.\n- Where the application under test comes from is declared rather than guessed, through the same ContainerSource model as TestFramework.Container: an image, a project path, or a directory. The resolved plan is logged before anything is built.",
